Node Exporter → Prometheus → Grafana metrics ke liye
Log Agent → Loki → Grafana logs ke liye.


Agent kya hota hai?
Agent ek chhota software/process hota hai jo kisi machine, application ya container se data collect karta hai aur monitoring system tak pahunchata hai.

Example: aapke paas 3 Kubernetes worker nodes hain. Har node par CPU aur memory information available hai. Monitoring system ko ye information dene ke liye agent/exporter ki zaroorat ho sakti hai.

Do common types samjho:

Metrics agent/exporter: System metrics expose karta hai, jaise Node Exporter.

Log agent: Application/container ki logs collect karke log backend tak bhejta hai, jaise Promtail (legacy) ya Grafana Alloy.

Har agent ka kaam same nahi hota. Node Exporter metrics expose karta hai; Promtail logs forward karta hai.



2. Prometheus kya hai?

Role: Metrics collection aur storage

Prometheus configured targets se metrics scrape karta hai aur unko time-series database mein store karta hai. Time-series ka matlab hai timestamp ke saath values record hona.

Example:

Time   CPU usage

10:00   35%

10:05   48%

10:10   91%
-------------------

Prometheus aapko batata hai ki CPU usage badh raha hai ya kam ho raha hai.

Query language: PromQL

Default port: 9090

Kubernetes mein: nodes, pods, application endpoints aur exporters se metrics collect kar sakta hai.

Interview: Prometheus data collect aur store karta hai; Grafana us data ko visualize karti hai.




3. Grafana kya hai?

Role: Visualization aur dashboards

Grafana alag-alag data sources se data query karke graphs, tables aur dashboards dikhata hai.

Example: aapko ek dashboard mein ye sab dikhana hai:

CPU aur memory usage

Kubernetes nodes ki health

Pod count aur restarts

Application response time

Error logs

Grafana inko ek hi UI mein dikhane mein madad karta hai.

Default port: 3000

Grafana apne aap Node Exporter se CPU metrics collect nahi karta; uske liye data source aur data collection pipeline chahiye.




4. Node Exporter kya hai?

Role: Linux machine ki metrics expose karna

Ye Linux OS ke CPU, memory, disk aur network jaise metrics expose karta hai, jise Prometheus scrape kar sakta hai.

Default port: 9100

Worker Node 1 → Node Exporter
Worker Node 2 → Node Exporter
Worker Node 3 → Node Exporter
             ↓
         Prometheus
             ↓
          Grafana



Promtail kya hai?
Role: Logs collect aur forward karna

Promtail log files ko read karta hai, labels attach karta hai aur Loki ko logs bhejta hai.

Example: aapke Java application ke logs mein ye error aata hai:

ERROR: Database connection refused

Promtail logs ko collect karke Loki tak bhej sakta hai. Grafana ke through aap error search kar sakte ho.

Important: Promtail deprecated hai. Naye setup mein Grafana Alloy ya koi supported log collector choose karna behtar hai.


Loki kya hai?

Role: Log aggregation aur querying

Loki logs ko store aur query karne ka system hai. Ye labels par focus karta hai, jaise namespace, pod aur container.

Example:

namespace="production"
pod="java-app-xyz"

Aap in labels se relevant logs filter kar sakte ho.

Prometheus metrics ke liye hai; Loki logs ke liye. Dono Grafana ke data sources ban sakte hain.

Aapke abhi wale lab mein Prometheus aur Grafana install hue hain. Aapne jo commands share ki thi, unmein Loki aur Promtail install nahi hue the. Isliye sirf Grafana dashboards import karne se Loki logs automatically available nahi honge.





7. Data Source kya hota hai?

Data source ka matlab hai Grafana data kahan se laayega.

Examples:

Prometheus = metrics ka data source

Loki = logs ka data source

Elasticsearch = search/log data source

MySQL = database data source

Aapke lab mein aapne Grafana mein Prometheus ka URL configure kiya tha:

http://prometheus-server.prometheus.svc.cluster.local

Iska matlab Grafana Kubernetes ke internal DNS se Prometheus service ko access kar raha hai.

Agar aap Loki install karte ho, toh Loki ko bhi alag data source ke roop mein add karna hoga.

Yaad rakho: Data source khud agent nahi hai aur na hi dashboard hai. Ye Grafana ko backend se connect karne ka configuration hai.




3. Kubernetes Monitoring aur Standalone Machine mein kya difference hai?

Ye dono alag deployment approaches hain.


A. Kubernetes-based monitoring
Aapke current lab jaisa

Is approach mein Prometheus aur Grafana Kubernetes cluster ke andar Pods, Deployments/StatefulSets aur Services ke roop mein run karte hain. Aapne Helm charts se isi tarah install kiya hai.

Fayde:

Helm se installation aur upgrades.

Kubernetes resources ke saath management.

Node Exporter DaemonSet se har eligible node par exporter.

Cluster aur application metrics ka centralized dashboard.



B. Standalone monitoring machine

Ismein alag EC2 machine par Prometheus aur Grafana install hote hain. Ye machine Kubernetes cluster ke bahar hoti hai aur cluster ke metrics endpoints ko network ke through scrape karti hai.

Fayde:

Agar Kubernetes cluster down ho, monitoring server alag hone ke kaaran kuch monitoring available reh sakti hai.

Ek central monitoring server multiple clusters ya Linux machines monitor kar sakta hai.

Monitoring workloads application cluster ke resources consume nahi karte.

Lekin monitoring server, network access, authentication aur scrape targets ki configuration manage karni padti hai.

Ek important clarification: Standalone machine ka matlab koi special software nahi hai. Ye sirf installation location ka difference hai. Prometheus aur Grafana wahi hain; bas Kubernetes ke andar run karne ke bajay alag EC2 par run karte hain.

